---
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Website Privacy | Total Tissue & Fitness"
  description="Information about inquiry forms, external booking providers, and video playback on the Total Tissue & Fitness website."
  noindex
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="WEBSITE INFORMATION"
    title="Privacy & your information"
    description="Prototype information only. This describes the current demo behavior and does not replace an approved production privacy policy."
  />
  <article class="container prose section border-top">
    <h2>Inquiries</h2><p>
      This proof-of-concept inquiry form does not send or save your information. Please use
      fictional sample details to explore it. A future live form will need an approved privacy
      policy and a connected delivery system.
    </p><h2>Booking providers</h2><p>
      Booking links may take you to Vagaro, Calendly, or another provider designated by the team.
      Those services have their own privacy policies and terms. Review them before entering personal
      information.
    </p><h2>Video playback</h2><p>
      Videos are not loaded from YouTube until you choose to open a video player. Playback connects
      to YouTube’s privacy-enhanced embed service, which is governed by Google’s policies.
    </p><h2>Partner dashboard</h2><p>
      The dashboard is a publicly viewable demonstration containing fictional records. It does not
      have real accounts or permissions. Changes remain in the current page only and reset when you
      reload; no records are stored in a database or browser storage.
    </p><h2>Questions</h2><p>
      The <a href={withBase('/contact/')}>contact page</a> previews the future inquiry experience. Existing
      booking pathways are listed on the <a href={withBase('/book/')}>booking page</a>. A production
      privacy contact will be added before the site launches.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
